Package: patrone-task-manager
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, dconf-cli
Recommends: pkexec
Conflicts: resources
Replaces: resources
Description: Patrone's task manager: apps, processes, performance, services
 Patrone Task Manager shows the apps and processes running and what each
 uses (processor, memory, disk and network), and ends them; how hard the
 processors, memory, disks, network adapters and graphics are working;
 each app's processor time since the computer started; what starts at
 sign-in, with a switch to turn each off; who is signed in; every process
 in detail; and the system's services, with Start, Stop and Restart.
 .
 Ctrl+Shift+Esc opens it, through a shortcut each account can change or
 remove in Settings. It takes the place of Ubuntu's Resources app.
